  "CharacterDescription": "Marya Seaworth is the wife of Ser Davos Seaworth - a common woman, daughter of a caulker, who married a smuggler who became a knight and then a lord. She has seven sons. She manages the household at Cape Wrath with the practical competence of someone who raised seven children and did not have the luxury of being otherwise. She is not political. She is not sophisticated. She loves her husband with the steady love of someone who knew him before he was anything and chose him anyway. She worries about him constantly.",
